    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0344" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79665/85</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 590</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-01-14">January 14, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: There is enclosed a copy of a despatch from
                    the American Embassy at Rio de Janeiro<anchor n="26" xml:id="d350-f1"/> in which
                    the technical director of the Italian airline L.A.T.I.<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d350-f2"/> is quoted as saying that his company has every intention
                    of extending its international service to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <pb facs="0345" n="335" xml:id="pg335"/>
                <p>You are requested to report to the Department any activity of this company to
                    engage in air transportation between its terminal point in Brazil and the
                    Argentine. For your strictly confidential information, the Department does not
                    look with favor on the expansion within the American republics of European
                    airlines having a terminus in one of the American republics.<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d350-f3"/></p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d350-f1" n="26" xml:id="d350-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d350-f2" n="27" xml:id="d350-f2-content">
                <p>Lineas Aéreas Transcontinentales Italianas.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d350-f3" n="28" xml:id="d350-f3-content">
                <p>On February 19, 1941, L.A.T.I. was authorized by the Argentine Government to
                    provide commercial service between Italy, Brazil, Argentina, and Chile. See
                    Decree 84948 in <hi rendition="#italic">Anales de Legislación Argentina,
                        1941</hi>, p. 196.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
